---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
---

<MainLayout
  title="Client & Server"
  description="Understand the relationship between clients and servers."
>
  <article class="article container">
    <div class="eyebrow">COMPUTING / NETWORK ARCHITECTURE</div>

    <h1 class="display-title">Client & Server</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      Two roles that make networked applications possible.
    </p>

    <div class="metadata">
      <span>ARCHITECTURE</span>
      <span>FOUNDATIONAL CONCEPT</span>
    </div>

    <section>
      <h2>01. Definition</h2>
      <p>
        A client is a program or device that requests a service.
        A server is a program or system that provides a service
        in response to requests.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>02. Real-world example</h2>
      <p>
        When you open a website, your browser acts as a client.
        It sends a request to a web server, which processes
        the request and returns the page or data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>03. Request and response</h2>
      <div class="code-example">
        <pre><code>CLIENT
  |
  |  Request
  v
SERVER
  |
  |  Response
  v
CLIENT</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>04. Related concepts</h2>
      <div class="related">
        <a href="/encyclopedia/http/">HTTP ↗</a>
        <a href="/encyclopedia/json/">JSON ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <a class="back" href="/encyclopedia/">← Back to Encyclopedia</a>
  </article>
</MainLayout>

<style>
  .article {
    max-width: 850px;
    padding: 90px 0 120px;
  }

  .article h1 {
    margin: 25px 0 10px;
    font-size: clamp(54px, 10vw, 100px);
  }

  .lead {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .metadata {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 18px;
    margin: 35px 0 65px;
    padding: 18px 0;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 9px;
  }

  .article section {
    margin: 55px 0;
  }

  .article h2 {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: 30px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .article section p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 2;
  }

  .code-example {
    padding: 22px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  pre {
    overflow-x: auto;
    color: var(--lime);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .related {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .related a {
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  .back {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 40px;
    color: var(--lime);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
</style>